# The Lambda training environment. Resolved for linux/x86_64 + CUDA, NOT for this Mac.
#
# Kept out of the repo's own pyproject.toml deliberately: installing this stack here
# would resolve a CPU/MPS torch and produce a lockfile that does not describe the
# machine the training actually runs on.
#
# Pin decisions, with the evidence behind them:
#
# * transformers is pinned to a RELEASE, not a main-branch SHA. The plan assumes
#   Qwen3.5 is main-only and carries a whole risk row for "main moves daily"; it has
#   shipped in tagged releases since v5.2.0 (2026-02-16). See docs/plan-corrections.md
#   RELIEF-1. Pinning a release deletes that risk rather than mitigating it.
#
# * flash-linear-attention and causal-conv1d are CUDA-only and must NEVER be installed
#   in the Mac environment: the Qwen3.5 modeling file dispatches through a bare
#   `importlib.import_module("fla")` rather than the CUDA-gated helper, so a successful
#   import on a Mac sends execution into Triton, which has no Metal backend.
#   See docs/plan-corrections.md DESIGN-3.
#
# * causal-conv1d is sdist-only (no wheels) and builds against nvcc, so the image build
#   needs the CUDA devel base, not runtime.

--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128

torch==2.11.0
transformers==5.17.0
accelerate
safetensors
datasets
numpy
sentencepiece
einops

# Fast path for the hybrid. Their absence is a 74%-slower step, and their presence is
# asserted positively at runtime by stack/verify_fast_path.py -- never by grepping a
# log for an absent warning, which is a check that cannot fail.
flash-linear-attention
causal-conv1d

# Teacher labelling only.
vllm
